{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"07/10/2026 11:42:23","profile":{"player_id":"139572","last_updated":"07/10/2026 11:42","fullname":"Kushagra Omprakash Ojha","short_display_name":"K Ojha","name":"Kushagra Ojha","gender":"M","dob":"09/08/2009","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"","nationality_id":"4","nationality":"India","nationality_short_code":"IND","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"1","text":"Batsman","role":"Batter"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"7","text":"Off break"},"writeup":"<p>Kushagra Ojha is a left-handed middle-order batter and right-arm off-break bowler from Jaipur, Rajasthan. Known for his ability to adapt his tempo across formats, he combines strokeplay through the off-side with power hitting against pace and spin.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Ojha advanced through Rajasthan's age-group ranks, eventually captaining the state Under-19 team during the 2025-26 domestic season. During that campaign, he scored 565 runs in the multi-day Cooch Behar Trophy and added 308 runs in the limited-overs Vinoo Mankad Trophy, earning his selection for the national youth team.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>He made his international youth debut for India Under-19 in July 2026 during the tour of Sri Lanka. In the first Youth ODI at Hambantota, he scored 92 off 67 balls to help chase down a 321-run target. Later in the tour, he scored 111 runs in the second Youth Test at Galle, rebuilding India's first innings from an early top-order collapse.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>In September 2026, Ojha was included in the India Under-19 squad for the home series against Australia Under-19, featuring in both the Youth ODI matches in Rajkot and the Youth Tests in Puducherry.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1163","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"India Under-19"}]},"international_debut":null,"international_last_match":null,"stats":{"format":[{"comp_type_id":"21","comp_type":"